## Setup swiyu-verifier

### Start Local Services
```
# Clone and navigate to project
cd swiyu-verifier

# Start all services
docker compose up -d

# Verify services are running
docker compose ps
# Should show: verifier-service (port 8083) and postgres (port 5434)
```

### Expose with ngrok (for local tests)
```
# Pre-requisite: Install ngrok and setup (auth)

# Expose verifier service to internet
ngrok http 8083

# Copy the HTTPS URL (e.g., https://abc123xyz.ngrok-free.app)
# Update the environment variable EXTERNAL_URL in docker-compose.yml
```

### Create a Verification Request

- Access swagger on http://localhost:8083/swagger-ui/index.html
- Create a verification request
  POST /management/api/verifications
  Payload example:
```
{
"presentation_definition": {
    "id": "simple-test",
    "name": "Simple Test",
    "purpose": "Testing basic verification",
    "input_descriptors": [
    {
        "id": "any-credential",
        "name": "Any Credential",
        "format": {
        "vc+sd-jwt": {
            "sd-jwt_alg_values": ["ES256"],
            "kb-jwt_alg_values": ["ES256"]
        }
        },
        "constraints": {
        "fields": [
            {
            "path": ["$.family_name"]
            }
        ]
        }
    }
    ]
}
}
```
- Get the `verification_url` or `verification_deeplink` from the response
- Use it (qrcode or deeplink) with swiyu to get the Verification Request, once you have a credential such as the [BetaID](https://www.bcs.admin.ch/bcs-web/#/), with a claim *family_name*.

### Verify verification request state

- GET /management/api/verifications/{verificationId}
  → Should change from PENDING to SUCCESS once the presentation has been sent from the wallet